WEBVTT

00:13.070 --> 00:16.730
Kuroe-senpai is talking to you on purpose.

00:17.120 --> 00:23.700
To make you tell her that 
you want her to forfeit.

00:28.660 --> 00:30.100
Kumiko-chan.

00:30.100 --> 00:31.700
Good job.

00:33.890 --> 00:37.510
<i>This is the last audition 
of my high school life.</i>

00:42.900 --> 00:45.260
<i>I can't let myself be distracted.</i>

00:52.050 --> 00:54.060
<i>I'm just going to play with all I've got.</i>

00:56.160 --> 01:00.810
<i>I'm putting everything I've done 
until now into this one moment.</i>

01:01.710 --> 01:02.980
Euphonium.

01:03.410 --> 01:05.710
Kumiko Oumae, third-year.

01:07.880 --> 01:11.800
<b>Episode 12</b>

01:07.880 --> 01:11.800
<b>The Last Soloist</b>

01:13.430 --> 01:17.340
We'll hereby announce the 
results of the audition.

01:17.340 --> 01:20.150
<i>The next day, the results 
of the last audition</i>

01:19.580 --> 01:21.030
First, trumpets.

01:20.150 --> 01:24.770
<i>of the year were announced as 
usual, with little fanfare.</i>

01:21.030 --> 01:23.370
Third-year, Reina Kousaka.

01:23.370 --> 01:24.210
Yes.

01:24.210 --> 01:26.980
Horn. Third-year, Michiyo Morimoto.

01:26.280 --> 01:29.320
<i>With the Kansai competition 
having born fruit,</i>

01:26.980 --> 01:27.870
Yes.

01:27.870 --> 01:29.300
Third-year, Rara Hitomi.

01:29.300 --> 01:30.220
Yes.

01:29.320 --> 01:34.910
<i>no one questioned the outcome 
of the auditions anymore.</i>

01:30.220 --> 01:31.880
Third-year, Sayaka Fukui.

01:31.880 --> 01:32.700
Yes.

01:32.700 --> 01:34.790
Those are our four trombones.

01:34.790 --> 01:36.280
Next, euphonium.

01:36.580 --> 01:38.320
Third-year, Mayu Kuroe.

01:38.320 --> 01:39.140
Yes.

01:39.140 --> 01:41.190
Third-year, Kumiko Oumae.

01:41.190 --> 01:42.130
Yes.

01:42.130 --> 01:43.320
Those are our two euphoniums.

01:43.880 --> 01:45.250
Next, tuba.

01:45.250 --> 01:47.160
Third-year, Hazuki Katou.

01:47.160 --> 01:47.880
Yes.

01:48.250 --> 01:50.000
<b><b>Music Room</b></b>

01:50.010 --> 01:52.280
Next, I'll announce the soloists.

01:52.710 --> 01:55.600
Clarinet. Chieri Takashita.

01:55.600 --> 01:56.590
Yes.

01:56.590 --> 01:57.920
Contrabass.

01:57.920 --> 01:59.350
Sapphire Kawashima.

01:59.350 --> 02:00.350
Yes.

02:00.350 --> 02:03.110
Marimba. Tsubame Kamaya.

02:03.110 --> 02:04.100
Yes.

02:04.100 --> 02:06.680
Trumpet. Reina Kousaka.

02:06.680 --> 02:07.680
Yes.

02:08.330 --> 02:10.380
Lastly, euphonium.

02:16.320 --> 02:17.870
Kumiko Oumae.

02:19.330 --> 02:21.020
And Mayu Kuroe.

02:23.590 --> 02:25.290
Be quiet!

02:25.290 --> 02:26.910
You two will have another audition,

02:26.910 --> 02:30.590
the result of which will be chosen 
by a vote of all other members.

02:32.970 --> 02:33.900
<i>She's right.</i>

02:34.490 --> 02:39.930
<i>If she's really intent on forfeiting, 
she would raise her hand now.</i>

02:41.390 --> 02:42.410
<i>And yet...</i>

02:54.230 --> 02:55.760
Pardon me.

02:56.660 --> 02:58.320
Is something the matter?

02:58.870 --> 03:01.550
Taki-sensei, um...

03:07.660 --> 03:09.490
Is it about the audition?

03:10.010 --> 03:10.730
Yes.

03:12.060 --> 03:13.460
I understand.

03:13.920 --> 03:16.830
But it truly was a difficult decision.

03:17.260 --> 03:20.830
I'm confident that both of 
you are fit for the soli.

03:21.350 --> 03:24.330
But given that you are the president,

03:24.330 --> 03:26.900
we need the entire band to approve.

03:27.440 --> 03:33.410
I'm confident in saying that I've elevated 
Kitauji as high as it possibly could go.

03:34.140 --> 03:35.190
So...

03:35.970 --> 03:38.450
Like the audition two years ago?

03:39.000 --> 03:39.810
Yes.

03:40.330 --> 03:43.460
In that case, I have a request.

03:43.860 --> 03:46.030
Please make sure no one can 
know which one of us is playing,

03:46.030 --> 03:49.220
so that people can make a decision 
based on our sound alone.

03:54.750 --> 03:57.260
I still have a lot to learn, don't I?

04:00.520 --> 04:03.810
My students are facing 
our work so earnestly.

04:04.420 --> 04:08.220
It's difficult to achieve your ideals.

04:14.000 --> 04:19.100
I'm privileged to have 
met students like you.

04:20.860 --> 04:22.330
Sensei...

04:22.830 --> 04:24.220
All right.

04:24.220 --> 04:25.660
I'll see to it.

04:27.500 --> 04:30.090
U-Um...

04:34.530 --> 04:37.470
<i>Please tap once more.</i>

04:40.080 --> 04:41.370
Hey, Reina...

04:43.300 --> 04:44.640
Is something wrong?

04:45.200 --> 04:46.430
Nothing.

04:47.430 --> 04:51.430
Would you be upset if I lost?

04:52.980 --> 04:54.080
I would.

04:54.850 --> 04:59.710
I've already decided I'm 
playing the soli with you.

05:02.570 --> 05:04.950
You said you've caught up to me.

05:06.970 --> 05:08.240
So...

05:11.190 --> 05:12.370
Don't let me down.

05:16.180 --> 05:17.410
I won't.

05:23.220 --> 05:24.870
I'm home.

05:24.870 --> 05:27.750
Honey, please talk to her today.

05:27.750 --> 05:28.880
I know.

05:29.680 --> 05:30.920
Kumiko.

05:30.920 --> 05:31.940
Let's talk.

05:31.330 --> 05:32.910
Dad, hey...

05:39.470 --> 05:41.920
Oww...

05:45.310 --> 05:48.700
Oww...

05:51.120 --> 05:54.120
<b>Career Survey</b>

05:51.120 --> 05:54.120
I'm on your side no 



matter what you write!

05:51.120 --> 05:54.120
Get 'em, sister!

05:51.120 --> 05:54.120
Mamiko

05:52.690 --> 05:54.120
Seriously...

05:54.120 --> 05:56.200
Stop coming home all the time.

06:03.540 --> 06:05.940
Too predictable. You're no fun.

06:06.420 --> 06:07.420
Huh?

06:07.790 --> 06:11.540
I was certain you would choose this path.

06:12.080 --> 06:13.840
You were?

06:13.840 --> 06:15.420
Taki-sensei was, too.

06:15.420 --> 06:16.740
Taki-sensei, too?

06:16.740 --> 06:17.850
Yeah.

06:18.180 --> 06:20.240
If you're done here, leave.

06:20.240 --> 06:22.090
I'll send you your documents.

06:23.990 --> 06:27.400
Grown-ups are amazing.

06:27.400 --> 06:28.960
Don't worry.

06:28.960 --> 06:31.520
As soon as you grow up, 
you'll be thinking to yourself...

06:32.550 --> 06:34.680
Those kids are amazing.

06:37.210 --> 06:39.380
Could you move that seat over a little?

06:38.880 --> 06:43.910
Oumae-san, Kuroe-san, 
please prepare for the audition.

06:39.380 --> 06:40.100
Okay.

06:44.680 --> 06:45.430
Okay.

06:48.560 --> 06:50.130
Kousaka-san.

06:50.130 --> 06:51.910
Please and thank you.

06:53.420 --> 06:54.230
Yeah.

07:09.900 --> 07:11.290
Kumiko-senpai.

07:12.480 --> 07:15.090
Please get the soli part.

07:20.390 --> 07:23.780
Kanade-chan, I want you to listen carefully.

07:24.350 --> 07:28.380
And I want you to vote for whichever 
you thought was better.

07:32.250 --> 07:33.160
Okay.

07:34.280 --> 07:35.540
Choose.

07:35.540 --> 07:37.900
The higher number plays first.

07:38.800 --> 07:41.570
Once the stage is set, you move out.

07:42.220 --> 07:43.430
Got it?

07:43.430 --> 07:44.710
Yes.

07:44.710 --> 07:46.260
Wait until then.

07:49.400 --> 07:51.470
Playing cards. Can you believe it?

07:51.470 --> 07:52.490
I know.

07:54.580 --> 07:57.420
Kumiko-chan, this is the last time.

07:57.420 --> 07:58.410
Huh?

07:59.930 --> 08:04.200
You want to play the soli 
with Kousaka-san, don't you?

08:17.020 --> 08:20.200
It's fine. I won't tell anyone.

08:20.950 --> 08:22.080
I...

08:23.890 --> 08:26.530
I have to apologize to you.

08:28.370 --> 08:30.610
I think I was scared.

08:30.610 --> 08:32.840
When someone good transferred in...

08:34.030 --> 08:35.100
I panicked.

08:35.540 --> 08:39.900
So I think I was pretending not 
to notice how you were feeling.

08:40.470 --> 08:42.610
You'd just arrived at our school.

08:42.610 --> 08:44.600
Of course you'd be in an awkward position.

08:44.600 --> 08:47.460
Yet I pushed it on you, 
saying it's a meritocracy.

08:51.410 --> 08:52.710
I'm sorry.

08:54.780 --> 08:58.690
You were putting it out 
there for me all this time.

08:59.300 --> 09:01.830
You were asking if I was really sure.

09:03.700 --> 09:05.140
You're overestimating me.

09:08.230 --> 09:09.510
Hey...

09:10.760 --> 09:13.920
Were you traumatized in an audition?

09:14.850 --> 09:15.950
Why?

09:16.510 --> 09:20.660
When I was in middle school,

09:20.660 --> 09:24.010
I got chosen for a competition even 
though I was in a lower year.

09:24.470 --> 09:27.210
And I went through some 
nastiness because of that.

09:29.050 --> 09:31.430
I noticed it when we were 
talking at the pool.

09:32.230 --> 09:35.710
You reminded me of how I was back then.

09:35.710 --> 09:40.350
Well, more like, you're 
fundamentally a lot like me.

09:41.980 --> 09:43.130
Yeah?

09:44.590 --> 09:46.850
I was thinking the same thing.

09:51.130 --> 09:53.530
I guess we're peas in a pod, huh?

09:56.150 --> 09:58.820
Though, actually, we aren't.

10:00.490 --> 10:03.530
It's Kousaka-san, isn't it?

10:06.810 --> 10:10.470
I changed when I came to understand Reina.

10:13.720 --> 10:14.950
I see.

10:15.780 --> 10:19.510
But I don't think that's 
necessarily correct.

10:20.490 --> 10:26.260
In my case, my friend quit 
music because of me.

10:28.300 --> 10:31.820
I was always the one 
chosen for competitions.

10:32.290 --> 10:35.050
She said it was fine.

10:36.000 --> 10:40.400
But in the end, she quit.

10:41.460 --> 10:46.470
So I truly, from the bottom of my heart, 
want to enjoy playing with everyone.

10:46.990 --> 10:48.210
I really think that.

10:48.830 --> 10:53.030
Compared to that, I don't 
care about auditions at all.

10:53.030 --> 10:54.230
Or about the gold.

10:57.020 --> 11:01.640
You're happy just playing with everyone, 
even if you aren't in the competition.

11:02.210 --> 11:05.100
But you can't play crappy on purpose.

11:06.440 --> 11:10.810
You don't mind stepping down if you're asked 
to, but you don't want to forfeit on your own.

11:10.810 --> 11:14.140
You don't want to lie to the performance.

11:15.470 --> 11:17.140
It's obvious.

11:17.880 --> 11:27.070
At the very least, the way you play isn't 
the way someone plays when they don't care.

11:32.640 --> 11:38.210
This is the place Reina auditioned 
for her solo two years ago.

11:39.790 --> 11:42.400
Reina and I made a promise that day.

11:42.890 --> 11:44.390
That we'd judge only the sound.

11:45.290 --> 11:47.970
That the better person should play.

11:50.020 --> 11:54.640
I've held that conviction for three years.

11:54.640 --> 11:56.110
I don't want to betray that now.

11:56.110 --> 11:58.600
That's my selfish wish.

11:59.850 --> 12:03.680
That's why I'm here to play 
with all I've got today.

12:06.060 --> 12:09.760
No sympathy, no compassion, no holding back.

12:10.340 --> 12:14.330
I want you to play for what 
you believe, too, Mayu-chan.

12:14.830 --> 12:18.930
I thought it was fine that you played.

12:20.910 --> 12:24.270
Why do you want me to play, Tsubame-chan?

12:26.330 --> 12:31.750
Because I feel like you're the 
real you when you're performing.

12:35.290 --> 12:37.820
Are you sure you want to help 
out your opponent so much?

12:37.820 --> 12:39.190
Don't care.

12:41.250 --> 12:43.480
I don't plan on losing.

12:47.060 --> 12:52.620
We hereby begin the re-auditioning 
for the euphonium soli part.

12:54.440 --> 12:57.580
Kousaka-san, you can begin 
when it's appropriate.

12:57.990 --> 12:58.830
Okay.

12:59.460 --> 13:01.810
Everyone, are you ready?

13:02.670 --> 13:06.100
Well, first candidate, please.

14:25.000 --> 14:28.420
Okay, next candidate, please.

15:48.160 --> 15:49.810
Thank you very much.

15:50.540 --> 15:51.890
The two of you, please come forward.

15:56.870 --> 15:59.450
You both performed beautifully.

16:00.530 --> 16:04.870
But only one person can play the soli part.

16:06.050 --> 16:09.350
Now, it's time to make a decision.

16:11.420 --> 16:15.550
If you believe the first performer is 
right for the soli, raise your hand.

16:28.440 --> 16:29.900
Thank you.

16:30.530 --> 16:34.900
Next, if you believe it should be the 
second performer, raise your hand.

16:49.400 --> 16:51.100
Two, four...

16:51.730 --> 16:53.750
Huh?

16:53.750 --> 16:55.170
What's the matter?

16:55.170 --> 16:56.210
Err...

16:56.210 --> 16:58.930
The first and second are tied.

17:00.290 --> 17:02.420
There should be an odd number.

17:02.420 --> 17:04.730
I haven't voted yet.

17:07.960 --> 17:09.530
Is that so?

17:11.550 --> 17:12.960
Have you decided?

17:20.930 --> 17:22.490
You won't abandon me?

17:22.490 --> 17:25.110
If I do, you can kill me.

17:32.630 --> 17:33.990
The first one.

17:38.470 --> 17:39.700
Understood.

17:39.940 --> 17:42.900
Now, if you're the first player,

17:44.510 --> 17:45.520
please step forward.

18:15.280 --> 18:16.360
President...

18:18.900 --> 18:22.570
Well, the euphonium soli part

18:26.100 --> 18:28.450
will be played by Mayu Kuroe-san.

18:33.610 --> 18:34.920
Kumiko-chan...

18:57.930 --> 18:59.060
U-Um...

18:59.940 --> 19:05.110
What kind of person is your ideal person?

19:06.360 --> 19:08.030
Let's see...

19:08.580 --> 19:11.470
A true person, I suppose.

19:11.920 --> 19:16.610
A person who's true in the real sense 
of the word is fair to everyone.

19:18.520 --> 19:22.090
What kind of grown-up do you 
wish to become, Oumae-san?

19:23.180 --> 19:24.610
I...

19:25.980 --> 19:29.610
I want to become someone like that, too.

19:32.040 --> 19:36.440
This is the best roster for Kitauji.

19:37.140 --> 19:39.830
We all chose this team together.

19:39.830 --> 19:42.930
No one can deny that those who 
are playing are our best.

19:43.820 --> 19:45.820
Let's go to the Nationals!

19:47.000 --> 19:49.510
Let's become one, and...

19:49.510 --> 19:50.350
Why?

19:50.910 --> 19:51.780
No...

19:51.780 --> 19:58.400
And we'll get the gold in the Nationals!

20:27.960 --> 20:29.490
Kousaka-san?

20:29.810 --> 20:31.270
She already left.

20:32.040 --> 20:34.220
She said she's sorry she 
can't help with cleanup.

20:37.410 --> 20:38.720
Reina...

20:38.720 --> 20:40.380
I was looking for you.

20:41.440 --> 20:43.040
Kanade-chan.

20:43.040 --> 20:44.880
What are you doing?!

20:44.880 --> 20:46.880
Again! And again! And again! And again!

20:46.350 --> 20:47.070
Kanade-chan—

20:47.070 --> 20:50.570
Why do you keep wanting 
to draw the short straw?!

20:50.570 --> 20:52.310
Don't you hate this?!

20:52.310 --> 20:53.760
Why do you...

20:57.020 --> 20:59.340
I wanted you to play!

21:00.810 --> 21:04.240
I thought you believed in a meritocracy.

21:04.240 --> 21:07.140
That and my frustration 
are two different things!

21:07.140 --> 21:13.900
I wanted a chance to play with you 
in the end, too, Kumiko-senpai.

21:15.010 --> 21:21.310
But after what you forced us to see, 
I have no choice but to move on.

21:24.810 --> 21:26.350
Thanks.

21:26.910 --> 21:29.640
You're a strong girl, Kanade-chan.

21:29.640 --> 21:32.320
Please don't trivialize it.

21:39.440 --> 21:41.690
I'm waiting at Daikichiyama.

21:47.390 --> 21:48.830
There you are!

21:49.640 --> 21:50.920
Reina!

21:53.160 --> 21:54.640
Here I am.

22:05.050 --> 22:06.180
Sorry.

22:07.530 --> 22:10.310
I'm sorry.

22:11.740 --> 22:13.360
Why?

22:13.360 --> 22:15.880
You have nothing to apologize for.

22:16.170 --> 22:17.390
No...

22:19.420 --> 22:21.070
No, I...

22:21.070 --> 22:23.640
You thought the first candidate was better.

22:23.640 --> 22:25.500
So you chose her.

22:25.500 --> 22:27.080
You made the right choice.

22:26.530 --> 22:27.720
No!

22:28.410 --> 22:29.700
That's not it!

22:30.200 --> 22:32.280
I knew!

22:32.280 --> 22:34.220
I knew that!

22:34.220 --> 22:42.370
How would I not recognize your sound?

22:47.910 --> 22:50.410
Do you regret it?

22:51.440 --> 22:52.590
See?

22:53.250 --> 22:56.130
I told you you're nasty.

22:57.180 --> 23:00.450
There was part of me that knew 
as soon as I finished playing.

23:00.870 --> 23:04.350
The hesitation I had from when I 
had doubts about music school...

23:04.350 --> 23:07.910
That showed in my sound, 
even if just barely.

23:08.940 --> 23:11.800
I knew that you could hear it...

23:13.390 --> 23:16.110
and that you would choose the best.

23:18.680 --> 23:25.430
Because you're special.

23:26.900 --> 23:31.450
I knew you wouldn't waver.

23:32.430 --> 23:35.420
That makes me happy more than anything.

23:35.420 --> 23:36.530
Kumiko...

23:37.290 --> 23:41.050
I want to hold my head up high 
for being proud of that.

23:41.620 --> 23:44.510
But knowing that about you...

23:44.510 --> 23:45.570
Kumiko...

23:45.570 --> 23:47.880
I wanted to win by being better.

23:48.520 --> 23:52.490
And I wanted to play with you in the end.

23:54.340 --> 23:56.860
I... I...

23:56.860 --> 23:58.670
That's not what you really want.

23:59.490 --> 24:00.880
It's not.

24:00.880 --> 24:01.910
I'm so...

24:01.910 --> 24:04.200
That and my frustration 
are two different things!

24:05.170 --> 24:06.210
Kumiko...

24:07.890 --> 24:14.100
I'm so damn upset!

24:15.450 --> 24:17.030
I...

24:17.030 --> 24:25.320
I want to do my best to 
be proud of this feeling.

24:28.800 --> 24:35.220
So that I can stand shoulder-to-shoulder with 
you, no matter how far apart we are.

24:48.730 --> 24:53.240
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

24:52.010 --> 24:56.010
<b>To be continued</b>
